      "statement": "Complete the yet-type polar question with final 未 and 呀.",
      "stageRecord": "未 takes the completed IP as its complement and projects a head-final PolP. It has scope over the perfective proposition and asks whether the subject has eaten by the relevant reference time or has not yet done so. 呀 then takes PolP as its complement and projects the outer head-final CP, contributing the utterance-level, addressee-directed questioning particle. Neither particle is derived by moving the verb or the clause. The resulting pronounced order is exactly 佢食咗飯未呀, interpreted as ‘Has he or she eaten yet?’; the pronoun's gender does not require a different syntactic structure.",
